  ans: 1,
  exp: "A forensic sexual-assault examination requires informed consent from a person with decision-making capacity. The examiner should explain each component, obtain permission for relevant procedures and specimen collection, protect privacy, and allow the survivor to decline individual components. Urgent medical care should not be delayed by police formalities.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Examine without explanation):</strong> Evidence collection does not justify bypassing informed consent.<br>• <strong>Option C (Require police permission for treatment):</strong> Medical care should be offered according to clinical need without making it conditional on police authorization.<br>• <strong>Option D (Treatment consent includes all forensic procedures):</strong> Consent to treatment does not automatically authorize every forensic examination or specimen collection."
