  ans: 1,
  exp: "Forensic evidence requires appropriate collection, labeling, packaging, sealing, storage, and documentation of each transfer. A continuous chain of custody helps establish the identity and integrity of the evidence. Biological specimens are generally packaged using procedures appropriate to the material, often in breathable packaging after suitable drying when applicable.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (One unlabelled container):</strong> This risks sample mix-up, contamination, and loss of traceability.<br>• <strong>Option C (Undocumented handling):</strong> Unrecorded transfers weaken the ability to establish evidence integrity.<br>• <strong>Option D (Wash samples):</strong> Washing can remove or alter biological and trace evidence."
